  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "How many pairs of like terms are in the expression $6p-3+5q-2p-3q+1?$",
  "worked_solution": "We write the terms of the expression as follows:\n\n$$\n(6p)+(-3)+(5q)+(-2p)+(-3q)+(1)\n$$\n\nThere are three pairs of like terms:\n\n- $6p$ and $-2p$ are like terms because they both contain the variable $p.$\n\n- $5q$ and $-3q$ are like terms because they both contain the variable $q.$\n\n- $-3$ and $1$ are like terms because they both contain no variable.",
